IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999 (Qld) -- the date arithmetic the rules need, kept in one small module so that
-- daydate is imported in one place only.
-- Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the version in force from 29 October
-- 2026). (c) The State of Queensland, CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- r 7 (note): "A time allowed or provided for under these rules is calculated according to the Acts Interpretation Act
-- 1954, section 38". That Act is not deposited. The readings used here (fork F1): a period "within n days after" a day
-- does not count that day, so it ends n days later; a period of years or months "from" or "after" a day ends on the
-- corresponding day of the later year or month (on its last day if that month is shorter); a period "starting on" a
-- day counts that day. No last day is moved for a weekend, a public holiday or a closed registry.

§ `Dates`

-- A calendar date, day first.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day n days after` x n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL x PLUS n)

GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day n days before` x n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL x MINUS n)

-- How many days from the first date to the second (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` a b MEANS DATE_SERIAL b MINUS DATE_SERIAL a

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before` a b IF `days from` a b AT LEAST 0

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is after` a b IF `days from` b a GREATER THAN 0

-- The corresponding day n months later (n at least 0). Where the later month is too short (31 January plus one month),
-- daydate rolls the date forward into the next month; it is brought back to the last day of the short month.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day n months later` x n MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the candidate` EQUALS `the target month`
    THEN `the candidate`
    ELSE `the day n days before` `the candidate` (DATE_DAY `the candidate`)
    WHERE
        `months counted` MEANS (DATE_MONTH x MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the target month` MEANS (`months counted` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR x PLUS ((`months counted` MINUS (`months counted` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the candidate` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY x) `the target month` `the target year`

-- The nth anniversary of a day (29 February falls on 28 February in a common year).
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the nth anniversary of` x n MEANS `the same day n months later` x (n TIMES 12)

-- The last day of a period of n days after a day, the day itself not counted (fork F1).
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of n days after` x n MEANS `the day n days after` x n

-- The latest day for an act that must be done "at least n days before" a day: the act's own day is the nth day before,
-- the later day not counted (fork F2: not n clear days).
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day at least n days before` x n MEANS `the day n days before` x n
